Zero-copy display: the flip event of a commit whose scanout flush carries a
fence (module parameter blob_flush_fence) waits for that fence as well as for
its vblank tick, and the commit itself no longer waits for it.

The host completes the fence of a flush when its compositor released the
buffer shown before, so the compositor here hears of the flip - and may render
into the buffer flipped from - only once the host no longer shows it.  The
earlier version waited for the fence in the plane update, before the crtc flush
armed the event: the event then came a whole refresh after the tick it was for,
and the compositor, two refreshes ahead, starved for buffers.

The event goes out at the later of the tick it is due at (the next one, or the
one just gone in the flip grace) and the fence, with the tick's count and time,
checked at the commit, at every tick and after every batch of host responses
(no fence callback: the event lock is never taken inside the fence's lock).
After 100 ms it goes out whatever the host did.  debugfs
virtio-gpu-flip-gate counts the gated events and their waits.

